 :adr/known-gaps
 [{:id :external-host-allocation-identity
   :severity :medium
   :status :open
   :detail "The JVM reference host enforces exact allocation start and recorded extent; other host implementations have not demonstrated parity."}
  {:id :legacy-wire-pointer-provenance
   :severity :medium
   :status :open
   :remaining-broad-providers 6
   :narrowed-provider-consumers 7
   :cross-function-slice-providers ["providers/pg_pool_consumer.kotoba"
                                    "providers/pg_pool_reset_consumer.kotoba"
                                    "providers/pg_portal_consumer.kotoba"
                                    "providers/pg_batch_consumer.kotoba"]
   :detail "Six helper-heavy wire providers still pass pointer/length values beyond the lexical proof. Three lexical consumers and four cross-function consumers require checked extents. Pool reset, portal and batch consumers prove read and write slices at every direct caller; malformed frames fail closed and dynamic out-of-bounds access traps."}
  {:id :guest-reclamation
   :severity :medium
   :status :open
   :detail "The bump allocator does not reclaim individual objects; OOM and retention are resource-safety concerns."}
  {:id :slice-contract-canonical-grammar-port
   :severity :low
   :status :open
   :detail "The CLJ/Chicory runtime owns the initial slice-contract implementation and fail-closed raw-op union. The byte-identical kotoba-lang, kotoba-sema and grammar catalogs still need one coordinated authority/pin update before other compilers may claim this surface."}
  {:id :general-ownership-borrow-system
   :severity :informational
   :status :not-current-design
   :detail "Capability affinity is narrow S2 and must not be described as a general Rust-style borrow checker."}]
